---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About - Chad Donohue">
  <section style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
    <div class="prompt">LOADING USER_PROFILE.TXT</div>
    <h1>ABOUT ME<span class="cursor"></span></h1>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
    <div class="box">
      <h3>█ MUSICAL FOUNDATION</h3>
      <p>
        My journey into the world of creation began with music. As a young musician,
        I learned the importance of precision, creativity, and the power of collaboration.
        Playing in bands and orchestras taught me that the best outcomes come from
        understanding how individual parts contribute to a greater whole. This early
        experience with composition and arrangement would later prove invaluable in my
        approach to software engineering.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
    <div class="box">
      <h3>█ SHIFT TOWARDS TECHNOLOGY</h3>
      <p>
        The transition from music to technology felt natural. I discovered that coding,
        like music, is fundamentally about creating something meaningful from abstract
        concepts. The logic and structure of programming languages resonated with my
        understanding of musical theory. I found myself drawn to the challenge of
        building digital experiences that could touch people's lives in the same way
        that music does.
      </p>
      <p>
        Over the years, I've honed my skills across the full stack, from crafting
        pixel-perfect user interfaces to architecting robust backend systems. But what
        truly drives me is the intersection of design and engineering—where aesthetic
        meets functionality, and where user experience is paramount.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
    <div class="box">
      <h3>█ HARMONY OF ART AND LOGIC</h3>
      <p>
        Today, I bring that same musical sensibility to software engineering. I believe
        that great code, like great music, should be elegant, purposeful, and accessible.
        Whether I'm building a design system, leading a team, or solving a complex
        technical challenge, I approach each problem with both creative intuition and
        analytical rigor.
      </p>
      <p>
        When I'm not coding, you'll find me exploring new technologies, contributing to
        open-source projects, or returning to my musical roots. The interplay between
        these passions continues to inform my work and keeps me inspired to create
        digital experiences that truly resonate with users.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-top: 3rem;">
    <p style="color: var(--terminal-dim);">
      > FILE LOADED SUCCESSFULLY
    </p>
    <p style="color: var(--terminal-dim);">
      > CURRENT_STATUS: Building the future, one line at a time
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
